    "markdown": "# Network Diagrams and Activity-on-Node (AON)\n\n\n\n::: {.callout-note}\nThis chapter is in preparation. It will be built from **Lecture 6 -- Network\nDiagrams** of MGMT-3105 and the `Critical-Path-Diagram.xlsx` worksheet,\nfollowing the same structure as [Chapter 1](01-Sustainability.qmd) and\n[Chapter 9](09-Cost-Estimation-and-Budgeting.qmd).\n:::\n\n## Learning objectives (planned)\n\nBy the end of this chapter you will be able to:\n\n- Build an activity-on-node (AON) network from a precedence table.\n- Distinguish the four dependency types (FS, SS, FF, SF) and use lead and lag.\n- Perform the forward pass and backward pass to find ES, EF, LS, LF.\n- Calculate total float and free float and identify the critical path.\n- Explain how the critical path changes when durations or dependencies change.\n\n## Topic outline\n\n1. From WBS activities to a precedence table.\n2. AON notation; predecessors and successors.\n3. Dependency types, leads, and lags.\n4. Forward pass: earliest start and finish.\n5. Backward pass: latest start and finish.\n6. Float, the critical path, and near-critical paths.\n7. Running case: the AON network for the RC-vehicle project.\n",
